      "message": "the handlers for regular vendor hooks are executed under the conditional:\n```\n  if (cpu_online(raw_smp_processor_id()))\n```\nsee tracepoint.h.\n\nI think there exist cases where a cpu_online(id) might be false during the scheduler wake-up path which was part of the motivation for so many of the scheduler hooks being \"restricted\". Are you ok with this handler being skipped in corner cases like this?",
