      "writtenOn": "2022-03-29T02:52:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "the hook is return the cpu_util, if the cpu is offline, it is unnecessary to get the offline-cpu-util.\nnow in kernel， there are three places where the function is called:\n1.\ncompute_energy\n    for_each_cpu_and(cpu, pd_mask, cpu_online_mask)\n          effective_cpu_util()\n\n2.\nsugov_next_freq_shared\n    for_each_cpu(j, policy-\u003ecpus)\n          sugov_get_util(j_sg_cpu)\n                  effective_cpu_util()\n3.\ncpufreq_get_requested_power\n    for_each_cpu(cpu, policy-\u003erelated_cpus)\n        if (cpu_online(cpu))\n            get_load(cpufreq_cdev, cpu, i);\n                sched_cpu_util(cpu, max);\n                    effective_cpu_util()\n                    \nIt can see that the it would not get cpu util of the offline cpu.\n\nabove all, I think it is unnecessary to set the hook restricted.",
